{"id":"word:hebrew:H4912","type":"word","title":"מָשָׁל","subtitle":"H4912 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, a pithy maxim, usually of metaphorical nature; hence, a simile (as an adage, poem, discourse)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to מָשָׁל (H4912) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 39 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"מָשָׁל (mâshâl) means properly, a pithy maxim, usually of metaphorical nature; hence, a simile (as an adage, poem, discourse) First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 5 12."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"מָשָׁל","transliteration":"mâshâl","pronunciation":"maw-shawl'","strong":"H4912","lemmaId":"hebrew:H4912","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["מְשָׁל֖/וֹ","מָשָׁ֑ל","לְ/מָשָׁ֥ל","הַ/מָּשָׁ֣ל","הַ/מָּשָׁ֥ל"],"morphs":[["HNcmsc/Sp3ms",9],["HNcmsa",7],["HR/Ncmsa",7],["HTd/Ncmsa",5],["HNcmpc",4],["HNcmpa",2],["HC/Ncmsa",2],["HNcmsc",1],["HC/R/Ncmpa",1],["HC/R/Ncmsa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, a pithy maxim, usually of metaphorical nature; hence, a simile (as an adage, poem, discourse)","usage":"byword, like, parable, proverb.","full":"H4912. mashal II. מָשָׁל noun masculine Isa 14:4 proverb, parable (of sentences constructed in parallelism , usually of Hebrew Wisdom, but occasionally of other types); — absolute ׳מ Ezek 17:2 20 t.; construct מְשַׁל 1Sam 24:14 ; suffix מְשָׁלוֺ Num 23:7-8 t.; plural מְשָׁלִים Eccl 12:9 2 t.; construct מִשְׁלֵי Prov 1:1 3 t.; — 1 proverbial saying , brief terse sentence of popular sagacity 1Sam 10:12 ; Ezek 12:22-23 , 18:2-3 , ׳מ הַקַדְמֹנִי 1Sam 24:14 proverb of the ancients. 2 by-word Psa 44:15 ; 69:12 ; וְלִשְׁנִינָה לְמָשָׁל Deut 28:37 ; 1Kin 9:7 ; 2Chr 7:20 ; Jer 24:9 ; וּלְמָשָׁל לְאוֺת Ezek 14:8 3 prophetic figurative discourse: מָשָׁל נָשָׂא lift up, utter a ׳מ Num 23:7 , 18 ; 24:3 , 15 , 20 , 21 , 23 (all of Balaam); Isa 14:4 ; Micah 2:4 (|| נהי ) Hab 2:6 (|| חידה ), (compare Job 27:1 ; 29:1 for same phrase under 6 ). 4 similitude, parable , Ezek 17:2 ; 21:5 ; 24:3 . 5 poem , of various kinds: the ode ( Num 21:27-30 ), the 3, 000 pieces traditionally ascribed to Solomon 1Kin 5:12 , didactic psalms Psa 49:5 ; 78:2 . 6 sentences of ethical wisdom חֲכָמִים דִּבְרֵי collected in the שְׁלֹמֹה מִשְׁלֵי Prov 10:1 ; 25:1 ( 10:1-22 :16 consisting of 376 couplets chiefly antithetical; Proverbs 25-29 chiefly couplets of an emblematic type, but also occasional tristichs, tetrastichs, pentastichs, and decastichs. To these are appended דְּבָרִים of a more mixed character as to size and content 22:7-24 :22, 23-34; 30:1-14 ; 30:15-33 ; 31:1-9 ; 31:10-31 ; the Praise of Wisdom 1:8-9 is prefixed, and an introduction to the whole 1:1-7 , in which the whole contents are represented as) משׁלים 1:1 , compare 1:6 . The references in Job 13:12 ; 27:1 ; 29:1 ; Prov 26:7 , 9 ; Eccl 12:9 are to the same type of wisdom.","rootNote":"apparently from 4910 in some original sense of superiority in mental action;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 5 12","keyReferences":["1Kgs 5 12","1Kgs 9 7","1Sam 10 12","1Sam 24 14","2Chr 7 20","Deut 28 37","Eccl 12 9","Ezek 12 22"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":39,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 5 12","book":"1Kgs","chapter":5,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מָשָׁ֑ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 9 7","book":"1Kgs","chapter":9,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/מָשָׁ֥ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 10 12","book":"1Sam","chapter":10,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/מָשָׁ֔ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 24 14","book":"1Sam","chapter":24,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מְשַׁל֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"2Chr 7 20","book":"2Chr","chapter":7,"verse":20,"en